<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Authors>Oslofjord Operations AS</Authors>
    <Company>Oslofjord Operations AS</Company>
    <Product>Sanity LINQ</Product>
    <Version>2.0.0</Version>
    <Description>Strongly-typed .Net Client for Sanity CMS (https://sanity.io)</Description>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <Copyright>2018 Oslofjord Operations AS</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/oslofjord/sanity-linq</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/oslofjord/sanity-linq</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>sanity cms dotnet linq client groq</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <AssemblyVersion>2.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <PackageId>Sanity.Linq</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>Sanity.Linq</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Sanity.Linq</RootNamespace>
    <FileVersion>2.0.0.0</FileVersion>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.0 - Sanity Linq library
1.1 - BlockContent library
1.1.1 - Improvements BlockContent
1.1.2 - Fixed bug where SanityLocale.Get() would not work with strings.
1.1.4 - Fixed bug that caused a SanityLocale&lt;object&gt; object to get Translations property with null for all values.
1.1.5 - Fixed bug in update
1.1.6 - Support for localized arrays
1.1.8 - Updated documentation
1.2.0 - Support for nested Includes / projections
1.2.1 - Extended tests and improved support for fluid/Linq includes
1.3.0 - Support for field aliases when joining / including
1.3.7 - Added support for weak references to SanityReference common type
1.3.9 - Added support for sanity _key field to SanityDocument common type
1.4.0 - Support for cancellation tokens
1.4.1 - Bugfix for weak references
1.4.2 - Support for "Contains" queries
1.4.3 - Support for IHttpClientFactory
1.4.4 - SanityFile type added
1.4.5 - Added support for choosing API-version
1.5.0 - Updated dependencies and support for source link, some serialization fixes
1.6.0 - Fixed support for queries with parameters against the CDN endpoint
1.7.0 - Allow for overriding JsonSerializerSettings for serialization and deserialization
1.7.1 - Fixed using correct serializer settings in client
1.8.0 - Maintenance release: updated Microsoft.Extensions.Http to a supported version (CVE remediation); fixed malformed line breaks in ToHtml/SanityHtmlBuilder output (now emits &lt;br /&gt;) (#75); introduced Sanity-specific exception types (SanityException base with SanitySerializationException, SanityQueryException, SanityBlockContentException; SanityHttpException now derives from SanityException) and switched argument/state guards to standard BCL exceptions (#72). Behavioral change: the concrete exception types thrown on some paths have changed - catch (SanityException) to handle any Sanity-domain failure.
2.0.0 - BREAKING: replaced Newtonsoft.Json with System.Text.Json (#71). Newtonsoft.Json is no longer a dependency.
  * JsonSerializerSettings is now JsonSerializerOptions throughout. SanityClient.SerializerSettings/DeserializerSettings and SanityDataContext.SerializerSettings/DeserializerSettings are now SerializerOptions/DeserializerOptions; SanityMutationBuilder.Build and the SanityClient/SanityDataContext/SanityHtmlBuilder constructors take JsonSerializerOptions.
  * Block content serializers receive System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode instead of JToken. SanityHtmlBuilder.Serializers, AddSerializer, AddHtmlSerializer, SanityHtmlSerializers and SanityTreeBuilder.Build are all affected.
  * Model classes should use [JsonPropertyName] / [JsonIgnore] from System.Text.Json. Newtonsoft's [JsonProperty] / [JsonIgnore] are still honoured for GROQ query generation, so existing queries keep working; reproducing them during serialization additionally requires the Sanity.Linq.Newtonsoft package.
  * Install Sanity.Linq.Newtonsoft to keep 1.x serializer settings, custom Newtonsoft converters, Newtonsoft model attributes and JToken block serializers working during migration. See MIGRATION.md.
  * Fixed: deserializing a dereferenced reference that carries _key or _weak threw an ArgumentException. Sanity emits _key for objects inside arrays, so this affected real documents.
  * Fixed: a schemaless (JObject-typed) field emitted a second, malformed projection alongside "{...}". Free-form fields now project as "{...}" only, and JsonObject/JsonNode/JsonElement are recognised as free-form.
  * Fixed: chained query operators repeated the ordering clause. The expression tree was traversed twice at every level, visiting the innermost call 2^depth times, so .OrderBy(t).Skip(5).Take(10) emitted "order(t asc, t asc, t asc, t asc)" and .OrderBy(a).ThenBy(b) emitted "order(a asc, b asc, a asc)". Results were already ordered correctly, so this changes the query text rather than what Sanity returns; update any assertions on generated GROQ.
  * Behavioural change: an explicit attribute name is no longer camel-cased. 1.x applied its naming strategy on top of [JsonProperty("MyField")], yielding "myField"; [JsonPropertyName("MyField")] now serializes as "MyField". Names already lowercase or prefixed with _ (all Sanity system fields) are unaffected.
  * GROQ output, mutation payloads and ToHtml output are otherwise unchanged, covered by an offline golden test suite.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>

	<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
	<EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
	<DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
  </PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">
		<ContinuousIntegrationBuild>true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
	</PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
	<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="8.0.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="8.0.5" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
